<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  path="/terms"
  title="Terms · Bronzla"
  description="Bronzla is free: no purchase, no subscription, no in-app purchases. The full medical disclaimer and terms of use."
  showWeatherAttribution={false}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <header class="container page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Using the app</p>
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p>These terms cover your use of Bronzla, the sun exposure app published by HMD Developments.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="container terms-body">
    <div class="term">
      <h2>Price</h2>
      <p>
        Bronzla is free on the App Store. There is no purchase price, no subscription, no
        recurring charge, and no in-app purchase of any kind.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="term">
      <h2>What the app does</h2>
      <p>
        Bronzla calculates a safe sun exposure time from the current UV index, your Fitzpatrick
        skin type and your SPF, and offers a timer, UV forecasts and a session log built on top
        of that calculation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="term">
      <h2>Medical disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Bronzla provides general sun-safety guidance, not medical advice. It does not diagnose,
        treat or claim any medical outcome. Exposure times derive from the World Health
        Organization and World Meteorological Organization's definition of the UV index (1 unit
        = 25 mW/m² of erythemally weighted irradiance) and published minimal erythemal dose
        values for Fitzpatrick phototypes I through VI. Sunscreen protection is deliberately
        discounted by roughly half its label SPF to reflect real-world application. Times are
        based on average values and vary from person to person. See a dermatologist about any
        concerns with your skin.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="term">
      <h2>Weather and location data</h2>
      <p>
        UV and weather figures come from Apple WeatherKit. Location is used only to fetch weather
        for your position and is never linked to an identity; you can also select a city manually
        instead.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="term">
      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Bronzla is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. To the extent permitted by law,
        HMD Developments is not liable for sunburn, skin damage or any other outcome arising from
        reliance on the app's guidance. Use it alongside, not instead of, your own judgement and
        professional medical advice.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="term">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms can be sent to the support address listed on the App Store page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

